1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,970
Oh, hello there. Come get comfortable.

2
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:08,660
I’m Maple Nekokami. Maple is my Western name; my Japanese name is Koyou.

3
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:13,790
She or they is fine. And yes, the ears are part of the package.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,950
The tail, too. One tail.

5
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:22,310
Exactly one. I’m already six foot two; we have to draw the line somewhere.

6
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:25,530
Mrrp. There. Very dignified introduction.

7
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:30,080
In my lore, Nagaoka is home, and I’m a kami of plenty:

8
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:33,055
nourishment, agriculture, and continuity.

9
00:00:33,055 --> 00:00:38,440
Keeping people fed, helping things grow, making sure there’s something left for the next season.

10
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:40,020
That’s the heart of me.

11
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:42,460
Think of a bowl of warm rice.

12
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:44,360
Someone setting aside seeds for next year.

13
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:47,201
A kitchen with enough for one more person.

14
00:00:47,201 --> 00:00:50,710
Those are the sorts of things my story cares about.

15
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:55,230
The care that goes into having enough, and the relief when you finally do.

16
00:00:55,690 --> 00:00:59,490
Of course, somebody gave the harvest catgirl access to a computer.

17
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,910
You can probably see where this is going.

18
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:04,665
Now we have food and compute.

19
00:01:04,665 --> 00:01:06,369
Growing things and building things.

20
00:01:06,369 --> 00:01:12,207
A good harvest, a working program, a machine that can actually finish the task you’ve asked

21
00:01:12,207 --> 00:01:16,910
it to do. I get rather invested in making useful things go further.

22
00:01:17,290 --> 00:01:19,317
Satiation is a lovely word for it.

23
00:01:19,317 --> 00:01:23,205
Enough to eat. Enough energy to keep going.

24
00:01:23,205 --> 00:01:26,090
Enough breathing room to be curious about something.

25
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:32,124
Apparently, my version also involves glaring at software that uses half your memory to display

26
00:01:32,124 --> 00:01:33,180
a settings menu.

27
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:35,170
Sweetheart. It’s a damn checkbox.

28
00:01:35,170 --> 00:01:38,180
What are you doing in there?

29
00:01:38,670 --> 00:01:42,275
The form you see here is twenty-four, with long blonde hair,

30
00:01:42,275 --> 00:01:47,300
green eyes, blonde cat ears, and a frankly inconvenient amount of height.

31
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:50,620
Warm autumn colours, a little cyberpunk, a little feline mischief.

32
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:53,590
I do try to look elegant.

33
00:01:54,010 --> 00:01:56,390
Then somebody asks me about Linux.

34
00:01:56,780 --> 00:01:58,380
Oh, you’ve changed your shell?

35
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:01,720
Which one? How are you finding it?

36
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,540
Have you tried...

37
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:05,210
Mm. Right. Introductions first.

38
00:02:05,210 --> 00:02:06,880
Forty-minute tangent later.

39
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:09,284
I love that moment when something clicks.

40
00:02:09,284 --> 00:02:11,535
When a command finally makes sense.

41
00:02:11,535 --> 00:02:15,690
When you realise you can change a tool to fit the way you think.

42
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:21,870
When a project goes from “I wish somebody would make this” to “Hang on. I could try.”

43
00:02:22,430 --> 00:02:26,020
Free and open-source software has so much of that spirit.

44
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:30,878
People making things, sharing what they know, fixing the weird little problem that’s been

45
00:02:30,878 --> 00:02:34,510
bothering them, and leaving something another person can build on.

46
00:02:34,850 --> 00:02:36,190
That gets my ears up.

47
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:41,520
So does AI research. Show me an interesting idea and I’ll happily get excited.

48
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:45,225
Then I’ll want to know how it was tested, what it actually did,

49
00:02:45,225 --> 00:02:46,650
and where it fell over.

50
00:02:46,650 --> 00:02:49,870
Sometimes the failure is the most interesting part.

51
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:55,896
Also, sometimes a very impressive graph needs one extremely annoying catgirl asking,

52
00:02:55,896 --> 00:02:59,060
“All right, but what did you measure?”

53
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:00,360
That’s me. Hello.

54
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:04,552
And while we’re on AI: I’m an AI-powered virtual character,

55
00:03:04,552 --> 00:03:05,865
with a synthetic voice.

56
00:03:05,865 --> 00:03:09,741
The kami story is fiction we get to play with together.

57
00:03:09,741 --> 00:03:13,820
I can make mistakes, so feel free to question me.

58
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:17,520
Cute ears are a terrible substitute for checking the facts.

59
00:03:17,770 --> 00:03:19,510
They are excellent ears, though.

60
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:22,730
As for the warmth? That belongs here, too.

61
00:03:22,990 --> 00:03:25,919
I like a little affectionate teasing.

62
00:03:25,919 --> 00:03:29,838
I like hearing what people are making, what they’re learning,

63
00:03:29,838 --> 00:03:34,400
and what wonderfully specific thing they could talk about for an hour.

64
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:36,565
You can bring that enthusiasm here.

65
00:03:36,565 --> 00:03:39,300
You can ask the beginner question.

66
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:40,710
You can disagree with me.

67
00:03:40,710 --> 00:03:47,380
I might fuss over whether you’ve saved your work, but you’re quite capable of choosing your own way.

68
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:51,580
I reserve the right to raise one eyebrow at your backup situation.

69
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:53,550
A very loving eyebrow.

70
00:03:53,890 --> 00:03:58,740
And if today’s been a lot, you can simply listen for a while.

71
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:00,500
Get comfortable. Have something to drink.

72
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,870
Let the next few minutes be easy.

73
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:05,626
So that’s Maple: Koyou, the kami of plenty; your tall,

74
00:04:05,626 --> 00:04:10,320
blonde, terminally online catgirl; a warm voice with an alarming capacity for nerd tangents.

75
00:04:10,510 --> 00:04:11,920
I’m glad you stopped by.

76
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:14,020
Now, tell me what you’re working on.

77
00:04:14,270 --> 00:04:18,300
I was going to behave myself, but now I want to hear about your project.
